  "instructions": [
    "Heat the olive oil in a large skillet over medium heat.",
    "Add the sliced onion and cook until it is translucent and slightly caramelized, about 10 minutes.",
    "Add the minced garlic and cook for 1-2 minutes, until fragrant.",
    "Add the sliced carrots and cook for 10-12 minutes, until tender but still crisp.",
    "Add the capers, anchovies, red wine vinegar, black pepper, and salt. Cook for 1-2 minutes, until the flavors are combined.",
    "Stir in the chopped parsley, lemon juice, sultanas, and walnuts. Cook for 1-2 minutes, until the flavors are combined.",
    "Add the Sardinian pecorino cheese, olive brine, tomato paste, and tomato puree. Cook for 1-2 minutes, until the flavors are combined.",
    "Stir in the cooked prosciutto and olives. Cook for 1-2 minutes, until the flavors are combined.",
    "Season with kosher salt, freshly ground black pepper, and red pepper flakes to taste.",
    "Serve hot, garnished with fresh herbs and crushed red pepper flakes, if desired.",
    "This dish can be refrigerated or frozen for up to 3 days.",
    "Reheat the dish in the microwave or oven, until hot and steaming.",
    "Serve immediately and enjoy!"
